{
  "_provenance": {
    "what": "The keys Home Assistant accepts in an MQTT discovery document: top-level, per component, and inside the `device` block. NOT a copy of what Vitals sends - it is Home Assistant's own accepted vocabulary, so a Vitals field that is misspelled, misplaced or invented fails the test that reads this file.",
    "where": [
      "homeassistant/components/mqtt/config.py - SCHEMA_BASE / MQTT_BASE_SCHEMA / MQTT_RO_SCHEMA",
      "homeassistant/components/mqtt/schemas.py - _MQTT_AVAILABILITY_SINGLE_SCHEMA, _MQTT_AVAILABILITY_LIST_SCHEMA, MQTT_ENTITY_COMMON_SCHEMA, _MQTT_DEVICE_INFO_SCHEMA_BASE (the device block)",
      "homeassistant/components/mqtt/sensor.py - _PLATFORM_SCHEMA_BASE (the sensor-only keys)",
      "homeassistant/components/mqtt/binary_sensor.py - PLATFORM_SCHEMA_MODERN (the binary_sensor-only keys)"
    ],
    "how": "Enumerated from Home Assistant itself, not transcribed by hand: the schema objects were unwrapped and their keys printed from inside the official container (see docs/integrations/home-assistant.md for the one-line script). A reviewer can reproduce it by reading those four files, or by rerunning the script against a newer image.",
    "enumerated_with": "ghcr.io/home-assistant/home-assistant@sha256:493a07e8f6530fc640223f4a0a5248f20a61ca2f718bb1d31efbf08a2c5ea28f (Home Assistant 2026.11.2)",
    "checked": "2026-11-20",
    "docs": "https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/mqtt/#mqtt-discovery",
    "note": "Home Assistant's sensor and binary_sensor discovery schemas are declared `extra=probatio.REMOVE_EXTRA`, so an unknown TOP-LEVEL key is silently dropped rather than rejected - a misspelled `state_topic` would simply do nothing. The `device` block is validated strictly, and an unknown key there discards the entire document, which is the failure this file guards against."
  },
